 ## Changelog
 
+- 2026-11-04: Structory no longer builds square terrain around its buildings (UNVERIFIED: written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain, not compiled, not run; +2 tests in `gen::structory`; the data analysis was run with `tools/structory_proto.py`).
+    - Cause (read from `structory.bin`): the templates bake a rectangle of grass / dirt into their bottom layers (60-96% of the footprint of the big ones) and fill their whole box with air; `place_piece` wrote both, and `beard` filled dirt up to 12 blocks (through water and lava too, `is_solid` is false for both) under every solid block, fences and torches included. Result: a square plinth, a square pit in a hill, dirt columns in lakes.
+    - Fix, all in `structory.rs`: the baked ground of a rigid piece is skipped (`base_run`) and the start is lowered by it (`base_depth`); the start height is the median of 9 ground samples over the footprint; air is only written under a roof (`roof_of`); the foundation (`GAP` 6, 8 for `beard_box`) runs under load-bearing blocks only (`bearing`) and stops at water / lava.
+    - Not done: a structure on an ocean or a lake is still placed (only its fill stops at the water); no overlap check between structures or with lakes / dungeons / trees (that is what Overlapless does, see below); paths (terrain-matching pieces) are unchanged.
+
 - 2026-11-04: Natural Temperature (Caesius_Leo, Fabric 1.2.1) ported, optional per world (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +4 tests: `gen::natural` x3, `menu` x1; `tools/natural_proto.py` was run against the mod's own classes: 6000 cases, 0 mismatches).
     - What it is: the temperature and humidity of the Overworld laid out in bands / rings / squares round an equator (8 modes each: default, simplified, linear, circular, banded, circular6, square6, discrete) instead of in noise blobs, so the biomes follow like the Earth's. Read from the mod's bytecode (its licence allows reverse engineering); `world/gen/natural.rs` is `MathUtils`, `TemperatureCalculator`, `HumidityCalculator` and `PainterCore`.
     - Proof: `tools/golden/NaturalHarness.java` runs the mod's own `PainterCore` on a JVM (class version patched 69 -> 65, Minecraft and Fabric stubbed, the two noises replaced by sine stubs) on random settings; `tools/natural_proto.py` (the Python twin the Rust mirrors) and the Rust test `matches_the_mods_own_classes` must give the same two numbers on `tools/golden/natural.txt` (168 cases, every mode). Mutating a constant of the twin breaks the check.
